.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}-4x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-1)) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =3\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534429 true] [17592186287871 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287872 13194139534429 true] [17592186287871 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534429 true] [17592186287871 1041 "field-1" 13194139534429 true] [17592186287871 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287872 13194139534429 true] [17592186287871 1110 #uuid "6018a901-83d4-586a-be85-47dd39a7b727" 13194139534429 true] [17592186287872 1034 "3\\pi" 13194139534429 true] [17592186287872 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534429 true] [17592186287872 1111 #uuid "7671c97c-2afb-50f1-8a52-8a5fdd530304" 13194139534429 true] [17592186287873 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287874 13194139534429 true] [17592186287873 1089 "q-348570" 13194139534429 true] [17592186287873 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534429 true] [17592186287873 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{4-1/\\sqrt{3}}^{5}\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}-8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534429 true] [17592186287873 1113 #uuid "300779b2-6c1e-5908-a102-8f06afbf164c" 13194139534429 true] [17592186287873 1145 "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x+17 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+({4}^{2}-{4}^{2})+17 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})-16+17 \\\\  & =(x-4)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{{x}^{2}-8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{(x-4)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x-4).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x-4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $4-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4-1/\\sqrt{3}}^{5}\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}-8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{-1/\\sqrt{3}}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{-1/\\sqrt{3}}^{1} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-arctan\\,(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{5\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534429 true] [17592186287874 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287875 13194139534429 true] [17592186287874 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287876 13194139534429 true] [17592186287874 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534429 true] [17592186287874 1041 "field-1" 13194139534429 true] [17592186287874 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287876 13194139534429 true] [17592186287874 1110 #uuid "03211610-2eaf-5d3c-a0c7-b3bfd62133db" 13194139534429 true] [17592186287875 1034 "\\frac{\\pi}{4}" 13194139534429 true] [17592186287875 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534429 true] [17592186287875 1111 #uuid "2fbe6fe7-068e-5354-8619-a9249365a932" 13194139534429 true] [17592186287876 1034 "\\frac{5\\pi}{4}" 13194139534429 true] [17592186287876 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534429 true] [17592186287876 1111 #uuid "5962bdf2-38a4-5364-bdcd-ce8c421c1bfd" 13194139534429 true] [17592186287877 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287878 13194139534429 true] [17